    "profile_text": {
        "body": "GE HealthCare Technologies Inc. is a public company headquartered in Chicago, Illinois, trading under the ticker GEHC. Its site describes it as a provider of digital infrastructure, data analytics, and decision support tools used in the diagnosis, treatment, and monitoring of patients. The company says it builds integrated solutions aimed at the healthcare industry's challenges, with the stated goal of improving outcomes for patients and clinicians.\n\nOn AI, GE HealthCare describes its devices as topping the FDA's list of AI-enabled medical devices, and cites more than 130 years of delivering solutions. It frames the future of healthcare as precise, personal, and connected, and says its tools are meant to help hospitals and health systems operate differently and to help clinicians make therapies more accurate and effective.\n\nLitigation data for the company records 290 cases in Illinois. No product listings, MCP servers, or individual lawsuits are recorded for it.",
